[38;2;124;124;124m**Proof.**[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mWe need to show two things: (1) A[X] is Noetherian, and (2) A[X] is Gorenstein.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**(1) A[X] is Noetherian.**[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThis is the Hilbert Basis Theorem: if A is a Noetherian ring, then the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mpolynomial ring A[X] is Noetherian. (Standard result: every ideal of A[X] is [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mfinitely generated, proved by considering the ideal of leading coefficients.)[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**(2) A[X] is Gorenstein.**[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mRecall that a Noetherian ring R is Gorenstein if and only if R_M is a Gorenstein[0m[38;2;124;124;124mlocal ring for every maximal ideal M of R. So it suffices to show that A[X]_M is[0m[38;2;124;124;124mGorenstein local for every maximal ideal M of A[X].[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Classification of maximal ideals of A[X].** Let M be a maximal ideal of A[X]. [0m[38;2;124;124;124mThen m := M ∩ A is a maximal ideal of A (since A/m ↪ A[X]/M is an integral [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mdomain embedding into a field, so A/m is a field). Let k = A/m. Then M [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mcorresponds to a maximal ideal of k[X] = A[X]/m·A[X], so M = (m, f) where f ∈ [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mA[X] is a polynomial whose image f̄ ∈ k[X] is irreducible (hence M = (m, f̄) in [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mthe sense that M is generated by m and a lift of f̄).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Reduction to the local case.** We have:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mA[X]_M = A[X]_(m, f) ≅ (A_m[X])_(m·A_m, f)[0m

[38;2;124;124;124msince localizing A[X] at (m, f) first inverts all elements of A \ m (giving [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mA_m[X]) and then localizes at the extension of (m, f).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSince A is Gorenstein, A_m is a Gorenstein local ring. So we reduce to the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mfollowing:[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m> **Claim:** Let (R, m, k) be a Gorenstein local ring, and let f ∈ R[X] be a [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mpolynomial whose image f̄ ∈ k[X] is irreducible. Then R[X]_(m, f) is a Gorenstein[0m[38;2;124;124;124mlocal ring.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Proof of Claim.** Consider the natural map R → R[X]_(m, f) =: S. This is a [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mflat local homomorphism: R[X] is flat over R (free, in fact), and localization [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mpreserves flatness; the map is local because m·S ⊆ (m, f)·S = the maximal ideal [0m[38;2;124;124;124mof S.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mWe use the following standard theorem on flat ascent of the Gorenstein property:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m> **Theorem (Flat ascent of Gorenstein).** Let (R, m, k) → (S, n, l) be a flat [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mlocal homomorphism of Noetherian local rings. Then S is Gorenstein if and only [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mif R is Gorenstein and the closed fiber S/mS is Gorenstein.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m> [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m> *Justification.* For a flat local map, dim(S) = dim(R) + dim(S/mS). A system [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mof parameters x_1,...,x_d for R and y_1,...,y_e for the fiber combine to give a [0m[38;2;124;124;124msystem of parameters x_1,...,x_d, y_1,...,y_e for S, which is S-regular if and [0m
[38;2;124;124;124monly if x_1,...,x_d is R-regular and y_1,...,y_e is (S/mS)-regular (by [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mflatness). This gives the Cohen-Macaulay ascent. For the Gorenstein property, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mone uses the type formula: when S is Cohen-Macaulay, type(S) = type(R) · type(S/[0m[38;2;124;124;124mmS), where type denotes the Cohen-Macaulay type (the dimension of the socle of [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mthe Artinian reduction). This formula follows from the behavior of canonical [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mmodules under flat base change, or directly from the structure of flat maps [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mbetween Artinian local rings. Since a Cohen-Macaulay local ring is Gorenstein if[0m[38;2;124;124;124mand only if its type is 1, the result follows.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNow we apply this theorem:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- **R is Gorenstein:** by assumption.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- **The closed fiber S/mS:** We compute S/mS = R[X]_(m,f) / m·R[X]_(m,f) ≅ [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(R[X]/m·R[X])_(f̄) = k[X]_(f̄). Since f̄ is irreducible over the field k, (f̄) is a [0m[38;2;124;124;124mmaximal ideal of k[X], and k[X]_(f̄) is a discrete valuation ring (DVR). A DVR is[0m[38;2;124;124;124ma regular local ring of dimension 1, hence Gorenstein.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mBy the theorem, S = R[X]_(m, f) is Gorenstein. This proves the Claim.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Conclusion.** Every localization A[X]_M at a maximal ideal M = (m, f) of A[X] [0m[38;2;124;124;124mis Gorenstein local (by the Claim, applied to the Gorenstein local ring A_m). [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mTherefore A[X] is a Gorenstein ring.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mCombining (1) and (2), A[X] is a Noetherian Gorenstein ring. $\blacksquare$[0m

